rota lap 4427, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; threshold, Standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal. The reading focused recovery on the actual parked files and kept the full tree still during verification.
obs Restored a changed-bound test beside the current pin advisory control. The control script imports plant_apply, changes the copied law to smaller and larger bounds, and checks that the advisory follows each one. A copied scanner fixed at the original bound loses that reading.
obs A separate frozen-reader trial passed all ten original checks and failed the two changed-law checks in the recovered control. The recovered witness refused the original ten-check control, then passed all thirteen checks after recovery.
obs Inspected all seven stashes and the current Incense transcript. All four distinct parked logs are already carried. The four equinox scans and the latest handoff page match HEAD; the loop has later changes. The older shared-pen, bound-reader, signing-law and shell-portability edits have landed or have later variants. Every stash remains intact.
obs Two missing shelf paths are restored from a148c34f573abf5f4dc67f70e264f63172ad8ece and a9c8b955f45fba60b0badbc810ba636dc17bb1a7. Later shelves already carry their account text; these originals restore the paths named by the earlier logs. The second is byte-identical; the first differs only by five proven link-depth corrections.
obs The duplicate REDS shelf remains parked because the published row already has its own shelf. The old doorway reach draft and fleet launcher remain preserved. The reach draft uses the earlier three-room population; the launcher predates the current watcher and clockout behavior.
obs The live shelf recovery exposed a repointer fault: one replacement changed all three identical targets, so its next queued occurrence refused. The regression also found an inline-code example being changed by the whole-file replacement. The writer now replaces one visible occurrence per scan row and preserves closed inline-code spans.
obs The repointer control now checks repeated-target completion, verdict, count, exact text with the quoted example preserved, and second-run convergence. The old tool failed four of these checks. The repaired tool and its twenty-five-check witness pass.
obs Recorded and closed the repointer finding at 20260909.042650. The initial package folded its row, then the final rebase brought an explicit dated-path gate reading. Withdrew that unpublished fold and kept a 154-byte closed row on the live pin; this log carries the full account. The withdrawn shelf remains in this seat's ignored recovery output and original local commit. The pin stays within its existing bound.
obs Ripgrep was installed outside PATH. Validation prepends its existing Nix store bin directory; host configuration stays as found. The cold transcript's seven stash detail lines match this tree's stash inventory.
obs No custody action was taken. The naming rulings, seed publish, scrub cache, identity and provisioning gates retain their existing status. No peer checkout or process was changed.
